From: pdp11-emu authors
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] PDP11: front panel export hooks (PANEL device)

Hooks for the PANEL device.  Its sources, pdp11_panel.c, pdp11_panel.h and
pdp11_panel_shm.h (the shared memory layout), are copied into PDP11/ by
simh/build.sh; see docs/SIMH_PATCH.md of the pdp11-emu project.

* pdp11_cpu.c
  - sim_instr: a local countdown, decremented once per instruction between
    the WAIT check and "inst_pc = PC", calls panel_sample () when it expires
    and stops before the fetch when the bridge requested a halt; then
    "panel_bus = 0" marks that the new instruction made no data cycle yet
    (a sample rebuilds the fetch from inst_pc, so ReadE needs no hook);
    panel_rearm () sets the countdown at entry and after every abort (the
    local does not survive the longjmp);
  - WAIT sampler: its own countdown, checked before sim_idle (a halt
    request then skips idling), and a sample after sim_idle slept;
  - sim_instr entry/exit: run state, register block, stop count;
  - the trap dispatch counts red stack, odd address, NXM and MMU traps
    (ADRS ERR);
  - bus capture, plain stores only: the virtual data entry points (ReadW,
    ReadB, ReadCW, ReadMW, ReadMB, WriteW, WriteB, WriteCW) record the
    virtual address with the D space bit, PReadW, PReadB, PWriteW and
    PWriteB record physical address, cycle flags and data in one 64-bit
    word, on the memory and the I/O page paths.
* pdp11_fp.c: the virtual address of the last word of the multi-word FP11
  stores (WriteI, WriteFP), which go through PWriteW.
* pdp11_cpumod.c: SR_rd reads the live switch register from the export.
* pdp11_defs.h, pdp11_sys.c: stop code STOP_PANEL "Front panel HALT" (a VM
  stop code, so SCP does not sleep 250 ms as after SCPE_STOP), PANEL device.
* makefile, PDP11/CMakeLists.txt: pdp11_panel.c in pdp11 and uc15.

Without an attached file every hook is a no-op apart from the stores.

The changed files are part of Open SIMH and carry its X11-style licence
(Copyright (c) Robert M Supnik and the Open SIMH contributors); this patch
is offered under the same terms.
---
